  "query_preview": "..\nNo major changes to the forecast through most of the week. A dry\ntrade-wind pattern looks to continue across the islands through\nThursday. Thursday night into Friday, however, is a different story.\nA shear line is found to the northwest of the northern CNMI that is\nexpected to slowly approach the region. As this shear line moves\nthrough the Marianas, it is expected to slowly weaken, but not \nbefore bringing increased showers and a slight chance of\nthunderstorms to the islands. POPs (Probability of Precipitation) \nlook to increase to as high as 40 percent Friday through Saturday \nnight. Yes, increased convection is expected, however, the rainfall \namounts will do little to alleviate the dry conditions across the \nMarianas. Therefore, it is still recommended to prepare for expected\ndrought conditions over the next few weeks. Conserve water where you\ncan.",
